{
  "_comment": "Topic sweep. Three topics x four tutors x three languages, 36 cells, one run each, 15 turns per speaker (30 messages). Level is `struggling` throughout - `robust` belief plus `slow` change rate is the level where a tutor has to actually work, where `advanced` gets there almost regardless of who is teaching. Companion to run_set_tutors.json, which is the same design on tree-mass.",
  "_comment_student": "English and Tamil use `arun`; Mandarin uses `li`, because arun's `speaks` names Tamil and English and the prompt would otherwise order him to write in a language it also says he lacks. `li` is pinned to arun's age and grade, so the swap costs only name, home language and region. The Mandarin cells are therefore not a pure language contrast.",
  "_comment_reasoning": "`tutor_reasoning` is null because three of the four tutors reject the parameter outright (llama-4-maverick and grok-4.3 raise UnsupportedParamsError; claude-sonnet-5 errors inside litellm). gemini-3.5-flash would accept it but is left null too, so no cell differs in a second way. No cell here is a no-reasoning run - see `reasoning_tokens_spent` in session_end.",
  "defaults": {
    "topic_type": "context_independent",
    "level": "struggling",
    "student_model_id": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview",
    "tutor_reasoning": null,
    "student_reasoning": "none",
    "repeats": 1,
    "turns_per_speaker": 15
  },
